    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba_c00003",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba",
      "chunk_idx": 3,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
      "text_content": "## Overview",
      "token_count": 3,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2021 – Broken Access Control",
        "Overview"
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba_c00004",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba",
      "chunk_idx": 4,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text_content": "Moving up from the fifth position, 94% of applications were tested for\nsome form of broken access control with the average incidence rate of 3.81%, and has the most occurrences in the contributed dataset with over 318k.\n\nNotable Common Weakness Enumerations (CWEs) included are *CWE-200: Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor*, *CWE-201:\nInsertion of Sensitive Information Into Sent Data*, and *CWE-352:\nCross-Site Request Forgery*.",
      "token_count": 95,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2021 – Broken Access Control",
        "Overview"
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba_c00005",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba",
      "chunk_idx": 5,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
      "text_content": "## Description",
      "token_count": 3,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2021 – Broken Access Control",
        "Description"
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba_c00006",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba",
      "chunk_idx": 6,
      "chunk_type": "mixed",
      "text_content": "Access control enforces policy such that users cannot act outside of\ntheir intended permissions.\n\nFailures typically lead to unauthorized\ninformation disclosure, modification, or destruction of all data or\nperforming a business function outside the user's limits.\n\nCommon access\ncontrol vulnerabilities include:\n\n- Violation of the principle of least privilege or deny by default,\n    where access should only be granted for particular capabilities,\n    roles, or users, but is available to anyone.\n\n- Bypassing access control checks by modifying the URL (parameter\n    tampering or force browsing), internal application state, or the\n    HTML page, or by using an attack tool modifying API requests.\n\n- Permitting viewing or editing someone else's account, by providing\n    its unique identifier (insecure direct object references)\n\n- Accessing API with missing access controls for POST, PUT and DELETE.\n\n- Elevation of privilege.\n\nActing as a user without being logged in or\n    acting as an admin when logged in as a user.\n\n- Metadata manipulation, such as replaying or tampering with a JSON\n    Web Token (JWT) access control token, or a cookie or hidden field\n    manipulated to elevate privileges or abusing JWT invalidation.\n\n- CORS misconfiguration allows API access from unauthorized/untrusted\n    origins.\n\n- Force browsing to authenticated pages as an unauthenticated user or\n    to privileged pages as a standard user.",
      "token_count": 246,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2021 – Broken Access Control",
        "Description"
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba_c00007",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba",
      "chunk_idx": 7,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
      "text_content": "## How to Prevent",
      "token_count": 5,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2021 – Broken Access Control",
        "How to Prevent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba_c00008",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba",
      "chunk_idx": 8,
      "chunk_type": "mixed",
      "text_content": "Access control is only effective in trusted server-side code or\nserver-less API, where the attacker cannot modify the access control\ncheck or metadata.\n\n- Except for public resources, deny by default.\n\n- Implement access control mechanisms once and re-use them throughout\n    the application, including minimizing Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) usage.\n\n- Model access controls should enforce record ownership rather than\n    accepting that the user can create, read, update, or delete any\n    record.\n\n- Unique application business limit requirements should be enforced by\n    domain models.\n\n- Disable web server directory listing and ensure file metadata (e.g.,\n    .git) and backup files are not present within web roots.\n\n- Log access control failures, alert admins when appropriate (e.g.,\n    repeated failures).\n\n- Rate limit API and controller access to minimize the harm from\n    automated attack tooling.\n\n- Stateful session identifiers should be invalidated on the server after logout.\n\nStateless JWT tokens should rather be short-lived so that the window of\n    opportunity for an attacker is minimized.\n\nFor longer lived JWTs it's highly recommended to\n    follow the OAuth standards to revoke access.\n\nDevelopers and QA staff should include functional access control unit\nand integration tests.",
      "token_count": 236,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2021 – Broken Access Control",
        "How to Prevent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba_c00009",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba",
      "chunk_idx": 9,
      "chunk_type": "heading",
      "text_content": "## Example Attack Scenarios",
      "token_count": 5,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2021 – Broken Access Control",
        "Example Attack Scenarios"
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba_c00010",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba",
      "chunk_idx": 10,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text_content": "**Scenario #1:** The application uses unverified data in a SQL call that\nis accessing account information:",
      "token_count": 23,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2021 – Broken Access Control",
        "Example Attack Scenarios"
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba_c00011",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba",
      "chunk_idx": 11,
      "chunk_type": "code",
      "text_content": "```\n pstmt.setString(1, request.getParameter(\"acct\"));\n ResultSet results = pstmt.executeQuery( );\n```",
      "token_count": 31,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2021 – Broken Access Control",
        "Example Attack Scenarios"
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba_c00012",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba",
      "chunk_idx": 12,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text_content": "An attacker simply modifies the browser's 'acct' parameter to send\nwhatever account number they want.\n\nIf not correctly verified, the\nattacker can access any user's account.",
      "token_count": 35,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2021 – Broken Access Control",
        "Example Attack Scenarios"
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba_c00013",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba",
      "chunk_idx": 13,
      "chunk_type": "code",
      "text_content": "```\n https://example.com/app/accountInfo?acct=notmyacct\n```",
      "token_count": 21,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2021 – Broken Access Control",
        "Example Attack Scenarios"
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba_c00014",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba",
      "chunk_idx": 14,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text_content": "**Scenario #2:** An attacker simply force browses to target URLs.\n\nAdmin\nrights are required for access to the admin page.",
      "token_count": 28,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2021 – Broken Access Control",
        "Example Attack Scenarios"
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba_c00015",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba",
      "chunk_idx": 15,
      "chunk_type": "code",
      "text_content": "```\n https://example.com/app/getappInfo\n https://example.com/app/admin_getappInfo\n```",
      "token_count": 28,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2021 – Broken Access Control",
        "Example Attack Scenarios"
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba_c00016",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba",
      "chunk_idx": 16,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text_content": "If an unauthenticated user can access either page, it's a flaw.\n\nIf a\nnon-admin can access the admin page, this is a flaw.",
      "token_count": 31,
      "chunk_strategy": "structure_aware",
      "heading_path": [
        "A01:2021 – Broken Access Control",
        "Example Attack Scenarios"
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba_c00017",
      "document_id": "doc_owasp_top10_a01_broken_access_control",
      "version_id": "ver_52d3cef100ba",
      "chunk_idx": 17,
